#
# Evidence for Tasks.md 3.3 and for the submission: production CRE enrollment is
# private beta, so a simulate run is what stands in for a live attested
# deployment. Three things to read for:
#
#   1. The TEE banner — confidential mode simulates, closing the second of the
#      two boxes Spike B left open.
#   2. The result carries `status` and `body` as well as the verdict. That is
#      the payload the proxy relays back to the agent: the trigger response does
#      not return it (CRE-3), and the proxy cannot fetch it itself, because an
#      x402 payment settles once and the enclave's call was it.
#   3. That result appears HERE, in the simulator's output, and NOT in the
#      response to the trigger POST — which returned 200 with an empty body in
#      0.3ms. That is what settles CRE-3 in docs/spikes/cre.md.
#
# The run passed sla: null, so the workflow took the status-only fallback and
# the provider's 2xx scored PASS. `tx` is zeroed and `writeError` null because a
# non-broadcast simulate does not submit the report.

